problems.problem:
Find all triples $(a,b,c)$ of positive integers with $a+b+c=10$ such that there exist $a$ red, $b$ blue and $c$ green points (all distinct) in the plane with the following properties:
- for each red point and each blue point we consider the distance between these two points; the sum of all these distances is $37$;
- for each green point and each red point we consider the distance between these two points; the sum of all these distances is $30$;
- for each blue point and each green point we consider the distance between these two points; the sum of all these distances is $1$.

At a secondary school, every class has an odd number of pupils. Furthermore, every pupil has a best friend (possibly from another class). Everyone is the best friend of his or her best friend. For the city trip, every pupil goes to Rome or to Paris. Prove that the pupils can be divided over the two destinations such that

(i) every pupil goes on the city trip together with his best friend;

(ii) for every class, the absolute difference between the number of pupils going to Rome and the number of pupils going to Paris is equal to $1$.

Find all functions $f:\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{Z}$ satisfying the following two conditions:

(i) for all integers $x$ we have $f(f(x))=x$;

(ii) for all integers $x$ and $y$ such that $x+y$ is odd we have $f(x)+f(y)\ge x+y$.
